  "description": "The application relates to the replacement of existing windows at 182C Drakefell Road, SE4 2DS, a residential flat located within a conservation area. There is no change of use proposed, and the property will remain in use as a single self-contained residential flat (Use Class C3).\n\nIn 2023, five windows were replaced at the property. The works comprised:\n\nTwo UPVC sash windows installed to the front elevation serving the living room.\n\nOne UPVC sash window installed to the rear elevation serving the bedroom.\n\nOne UPVC casement window installed to the rear elevation serving the bathroom.\n\nOne UPVC casement window installed to the rear elevation serving the kitchen.\n\nRetrospective planning permission is sought for the three rear elevation windows (one UPVC sash window to the bedroom and two UPVC casement windows to the bathroom and kitchen). These replacements replicate the original window openings with no alteration to the size of openings, structural works, or changes to the external layout. The works are like-for-like in terms of positioning and function.\n\nIn respect of the front elevation, it is proposed to remove the two existing UPVC sash windows and replace them with timber sash windows of traditional design to better preserve and enhance the character and appearance of the conservation area. The proposed timber sash windows will match the original proportions, glazing bar arrangement, and detailing appropriate to the building and surrounding properties. There will be no alteration to the window openings or overall façade arrangement.\n\nNo extensions, additional openings, or other external alterations are proposed. The application relates solely to the regularisation of the three rear replacement windows and the proposed replacement of the two front UPVC sash windows with timber sash windows.",
